IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `doga-owner`

-- Dog Act 1976 (WA), with the Dog Regulations 2013 -- the Q&A layer: the questions people ask, with the seat and the
-- situation as parameters, so that one deployment serves every seat and the question form drops the questions that do
-- not arise.
--
-- SEATS (`my role`, the first input of every exported question, "Which of these describes you"):
--   * the person who owns or keeps a dog -- the baseline's seat (Chloe and Mochi, c075), whose 16 questions are asked
--     here by calling the baseline's functions in doga-owner.l4;
--   * a person whom a dog attacked, chased or threatened, or whose animal it did -- who asks whether the dog can be
--     declared dangerous (s 33E; provoked behaviour is not an attack, s 3(1)), whether it already is a dangerous dog
--     (s 3(1)), and whether it was lawfully where it was (ss 31, 32).
-- A question about another role answers `does not arise for you` without reading any other input. The local
-- government, its registration officer, an authorised person and the State Administrative Tribunal are never seats:
-- what they may or must do appears as what it means for the person asking.
--
-- SITUATIONS (design D8 of the graffiti encoding): within a role, a question that arises only in a situation takes that
-- situation's fact straight after `my role`, and when it does not hold answers `does not arise for you` without reading
-- anything else. The questions of one situation share one input, character for character. All are the owner's, and
-- all are BOOLEAN, FALSE being the value that does not hold:
--   * `I have been given notice that my dog is declared dangerous`: the s 33F(2) and (3) questions, which run from the
--     notice;
--   * `I had my dog sterilised after registering it`: the r 19 refund;
--   * `my dog has been microchipped`: the s 23 notice of the microchip details;
--   * `I am said to have committed an offence under this Act`: the three penalty questions (ss 7(1), 21(2), 22(2),
--     r 33).
-- A question that arises in every situation of its role (is my dog dangerous, must it be registered, the fee and the
-- term, the microchip duty, public places, could it be declared dangerous) takes no situation input, and the person
-- attacked has none: every question of that role arises for every such person. The baseline's facts about the dog
-- (registered, sterilised, microchipped, declared dangerous) stay in its `Dog` record and are not repeated as
-- situations, which could contradict it; the microchip situation is taken only by the s 23 question, which does not
-- take the record.
--
-- No exported question takes a DEONTIC or EVENT input. The baseline's `Dog` record is taken as the baseline takes it.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md, "Q&A layer (seat and situations as parameters)".

§ `Dog Act 1976 (WA) -- the questions people ask`

§§ `Who is asking, and the shape of the answers`

DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `I own or keep a dog`
    `A dog has attacked, chased or threatened me or my animal`

DECLARE `Yes or no` IS ONE OF
    yes
    no
    `does not arise for you`

DECLARE `Amount` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    amount HAS dollars IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Date answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `by` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE

DECLARE `Day answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `it takes effect on` HAS `the day` IS A DATE

-- The baseline's own enumerations, carried with `does not arise for you`.
DECLARE `Registration answer, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the answer` IS A `Registration answer`

DECLARE `Refusal answer, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the answer` IS A `Refusal answer`

DECLARE `Fee answer, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the answer` IS A `Fee answer`

DECLARE `Registration end, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the answer` IS A `Registration end`

DECLARE `Microchip answer, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the answer` IS A `Microchip answer`

DECLARE `Microchip notice, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the answer` IS A `Microchip notice`

DECLARE `Public place answer, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the answer` IS A `Public place answer`

DECLARE `Declaration answer, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the answer` IS A `Declaration answer`

§§ `Helpers`

GIVEN `it holds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`yes if` `it holds` MEANS
    IF `it holds` THEN yes ELSE no

§§ `For the person who owns or keeps a dog (the baseline's seat)`

-- Each question calls the baseline's function of the same subject (doga-owner.l4) and restates no rule: for this
-- role, and where its situation holds, its answer is the baseline's, carried in the answer types above. s 3(1):
-- "owner" includes every person who keeps the dog or has it in their possession or custody.

§§§ `ss 3, 7, 16 -- is my dog dangerous, must it be registered, can the shire refuse`

@export Is my dog a "dangerous dog" under the Dog Act 1976 (WA) (s 3(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `dog` IS A Dog @desc Your dog
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my dog a dangerous dog under the Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own or keep a dog` THEN `yes if` (`Is my dog a dangerous dog` `dog`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must I register my dog (Dog Act 1976 (WA) s 7)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `dog` IS A Dog @desc Your dog
GIVETH A `Registration answer, if it arises`
`Must my dog be registered` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own or keep a dog` THEN `the answer is` (`Must I register my dog` `dog`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can the local government refuse to register my dog (Dog Act 1976 (WA) s 16(3), (3A))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `dog` IS A Dog @desc Your dog
      `banned by a s 46A(2) order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court order under s 46A(2) bans you from owning or keeping a dog
      `2 or more offences in the last 3 years` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, in the last 3 years, you were convicted of or paid a modified penalty for 2 or more offences under the Dog Act, the Cat Act 2011 or the Animal Welfare Act 2002
      `shown to be destructive, mischievous or diseased` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the local government is satisfied the dog is destructive, unduly mischievous, or has a contagious or infectious disease
      `the shire is satisfied it will be effectively confined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the local government is satisfied the dog is or will be effectively confined at the premises where it is kept
GIVETH A `Refusal answer, if it arises`
`Can the local government refuse to register my dog` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own or keep a dog` THEN `the answer is` (`Can the shire refuse to register my dog` `dog` `banned by a s 46A(2) order` `2 or more offences in the last 3 years` `shown to be destructive, mischievous or diseased` `the shire is satisfied it will be effectively confined`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 15, Regulations rr 17-20 -- the fee, how long it lasts, the refund`

@export How much is the registration fee for my dog (Dog Act 1976 (WA) s 15; Dog Regulations 2013 r 17)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `dog` IS A Dog @desc Your dog
      `I am an eligible pensioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an eligible pensioner under the Rates and Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Act 1992 s 3(1)
      `the term` IS A Term @desc The registration period: one year, three years or the dog's lifetime
      `first registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this is the dog's first registration
      `date of effect` IS A DATE @desc The date the registration takes effect (the date in the registration certificate from which it has effect), ISO 8601
      `local government discount` IS A NUMBER @desc Any discount in dollars the local government gives under s 15(4A); 0 if none
GIVETH A `Fee answer, if it arises`
`What registration fee must I pay for my dog` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own or keep a dog` THEN `the answer is` (`How much is the registration fee` `dog` `I am an eligible pensioner` `the term` `first registration` `date of effect` `local government discount`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export When does my dog's registration end (Dog Act 1976 (WA) s 15(2), (3A))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `dog` IS A Dog @desc Your dog
      `the term` IS A Term @desc The registration period: one year, three years or the dog's lifetime
      `date of effect` IS A DATE @desc The date the registration takes effect (the date in the registration certificate from which it has effect), ISO 8601
GIVETH A `Registration end, if it arises`
`When will my dog's registration end` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own or keep a dog` THEN `the answer is` (`When does my dog's registration end` `dog` `the term` `date of effect`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What refund do I get if I sterilise my dog after registering it (Dog Regulations 2013 r 19)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I had my dog sterilised after registering it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your dog was sterilised during a registration you had already paid for (Dog Regulations 2013 r 19)
      `dog` IS A Dog @desc Your dog
      `I am an eligible pensioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an eligible pensioner under the Rates and Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Act 1992 s 3(1)
      `the term` IS A Term @desc The registration period: one year, three years or the dog's lifetime
      `fee paid` IS A NUMBER @desc The registration fee you paid, in dollars
      `year of the term sterilised in` IS A NUMBER @desc In which year of the registration the dog was sterilised: 1, 2, 3 or later
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What refund do I get for sterilising my dog after registering it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own or keep a dog` THEN
        IF `I had my dog sterilised after registering it`
        THEN `amount` (`What refund do I get for sterilising my dog` `dog` `I am an eligible pensioner` `the term` `fee paid` `year of the term sterilised in`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 21-23 -- the microchip`

@export Must my dog be microchipped (Dog Act 1976 (WA) ss 21, 22)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `dog` IS A Dog @desc Your dog
      `in a s 22(3) period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a dog declared dangerous: whether it is within 7 days of the declaration notice, or an objection or review is pending or decided within the last 7 days
GIVETH A `Microchip answer, if it arises`
`Must my dog have a microchip` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own or keep a dog` THEN `the answer is` (`Must my dog be microchipped` `dog` `in a s 22(3) period`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export By when must I tell the local government my dog's microchip details (Dog Act 1976 (WA) s 23)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my dog has been microchipped` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your dog has been implanted with a microchip (the question of telling the local government its details arises only then)
      `date microchipped` IS A DATE @desc The date the dog was microchipped, ISO 8601
      `details given with a registration application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the microchip company and number have been or will be given with an application to register the dog
GIVETH A `Microchip notice, if it arises`
`By when must I tell the local government my dog's microchip details` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own or keep a dog` THEN
        IF `my dog has been microchipped`
        THEN `the answer is` (`By when must I give the microchip details` `date microchipped` `details given with a registration application`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 30-32 -- in a public place`

@export Is my dog lawfully in this public place (Dog Act 1976 (WA) ss 31, 32; Dog Regulations 2013 r 27)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `dog` IS A Dog @desc Your dog
      `the place` IS A Place @desc What kind of public place it is, as the local government has specified it
      `in the metropolitan region` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the place is in the metropolitan region (Planning and Development Act 2005 s 4)
      `in a townsite` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the place is in a townsite as defined in s 3(1)
      `the control` IS A Control @desc How the dog is being controlled
      `leash length in metres` IS A NUMBER @desc The length of the leash used or carried, in metres from the base of the dog's neck
      `at a show, trial, stock work, hunt or sporting purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether one of the s 31(2)(d)-(h) activities applies: a show, an obedience trial or class, working stock, a foxhound pack, retrieving or duck hunting
GIVETH A `Public place answer, if it arises`
`Is my dog lawfully where it is in this public place` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own or keep a dog` THEN `the answer is` (`Is my dog lawfully in this public place` `dog` `the place` `in the metropolitan region` `in a townsite` `the control` `leash length in metres` `at a show, trial, stock work, hunt or sporting purpose`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must my dog wear a collar with its registration tag in this public place (Dog Act 1976 (WA) s 30)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `dog` IS A Dog @desc Your dog
      `at a show, sporting purpose, obedience trial or race` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the dog is being exhibited, trained for or taking part in a customary sporting purpose, an obedience trial or class, or a licensed greyhound race (s 30(3))
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must my dog wear its collar and registration tag here` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own or keep a dog` THEN `yes if` (`Must my dog wear its registration tag in public` `dog` `at a show, sporting purpose, obedience trial or race`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 33E, 33F -- a dangerous dog declaration`

@export Can my dog be declared a dangerous dog for what it did (Dog Act 1976 (WA) s 33E)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `what happened` IS AN Incident @desc What the dog did
GIVETH A `Declaration answer, if it arises`
`Could my dog be declared a dangerous dog` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own or keep a dog` THEN `the answer is` (`Can my dog be declared dangerous` `what happened`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export By when must I object to, or seek review of, the dangerous dog declaration (Dog Act 1976 (WA) s 33F(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been given notice that my dog is declared dangerous` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the local government has given you notice of a declaration under s 33E(1) that your dog is a dangerous dog
      `date notice given` IS A DATE @desc The date the declaration notice was given to you, ISO 8601
GIVETH A `Date answer`
`By when must I object to the dangerous dog declaration` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own or keep a dog` THEN
        IF `I have been given notice that my dog is declared dangerous`
        THEN `by` (`By when must I object to the declaration` `date notice given`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export When does the dangerous dog declaration take effect, even if I object (Dog Act 1976 (WA) s 33F(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been given notice that my dog is declared dangerous` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the local government has given you notice of a declaration under s 33E(1) that your dog is a dangerous dog
      `date notice given` IS A DATE @desc The date the declaration notice was given to you, ISO 8601
GIVETH A `Day answer`
`When does the dangerous dog declaration take effect` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own or keep a dog` THEN
        IF `I have been given notice that my dog is declared dangerous`
        THEN `it takes effect on` (`When does the declaration take effect` `date notice given`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 7, 21, 22, Regulations r 33 -- penalties`

@export What is the most I can be fined for keeping my dog unregistered (Dog Act 1976 (WA) s 7(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am said to have committed an offence under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been charged with, or given an infringement notice for, an offence under the Dog Act 1976 (the penalty questions arise only then)
      `dog` IS A Dog @desc Your dog
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most I can be fined for keeping my dog unregistered` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own or keep a dog` THEN
        IF `I am said to have committed an offence under this Act`
        THEN `amount` (`What is the most I can be fined for an unregistered dog` `dog`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the infringement notice amount for an unregistered dog (Dog Regulations 2013 r 33, item 1)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am said to have committed an offence under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been charged with, or given an infringement notice for, an offence under the Dog Act 1976 (the penalty questions arise only then)
      `dog` IS A Dog @desc Your dog
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the infringement notice amount for my unregistered dog` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own or keep a dog` THEN
        IF `I am said to have committed an offence under this Act`
        THEN `amount` (`What is the infringement amount for an unregistered dog` `dog`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most I can be fined for not microchipping my dog (Dog Act 1976 (WA) ss 21(2), 22(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am said to have committed an offence under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been charged with, or given an infringement notice for, an offence under the Dog Act 1976 (the penalty questions arise only then)
      `dog` IS A Dog @desc Your dog
      `in a s 22(3) period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a dog declared dangerous: whether it is within 7 days of the declaration notice, or an objection or review is pending or decided within the last 7 days
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most I can be fined for not having my dog microchipped` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own or keep a dog` THEN
        IF `I am said to have committed an offence under this Act`
        THEN `amount` (`What is the most I can be fined for not microchipping` `dog` `in a s 22(3) period`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For a person whom a dog attacked, chased or threatened, or whose animal it did (ss 3, 31, 32, 33E)`

-- The person on the other side of an incident asks whether the dog can be declared dangerous (s 33E(1); provoked
-- behaviour is not an attack, s 3(1)), whether it already is one (s 3(1)), and whether it was lawfully where it was
-- (ss 31, 32). Each question calls the baseline's function on the dog and the place as that person knows them. The
-- owner's liability for the attack (s 33D) is not in the baseline and is not encoded here.

§§§ `ss 3, 33E -- the dog`

@export Can the dog be declared a dangerous dog for what it did to me or my animal (Dog Act 1976 (WA) ss 3(1), 33E)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `what the dog did` IS AN Incident @desc What the dog did to you or your animal
GIVETH A `Declaration answer, if it arises`
`Can the dog that attacked, chased or threatened me be declared dangerous` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `A dog has attacked, chased or threatened me or my animal` THEN `the answer is` (`Can my dog be declared dangerous` `what the dog did`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is the dog already a "dangerous dog" under the Dog Act 1976 (WA) (s 3(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the dog` IS A Dog @desc The dog, as far as you know it: its breed, whether it has been declared dangerous, and whether it guards others' premises
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is the dog already a dangerous dog under the Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `A dog has attacked, chased or threatened me or my animal` THEN `yes if` (`Is my dog a dangerous dog` `the dog`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 31, 32 -- where it happened`

@export Was the dog lawfully in the public place where it happened (Dog Act 1976 (WA) ss 31, 32)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the dog` IS A Dog @desc The dog, as far as you know it: its breed, whether it has been declared dangerous, and whether it guards others' premises
      `the place` IS A Place @desc What kind of public place it is, as the local government has specified it
      `in the metropolitan region` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the place is in the metropolitan region (Planning and Development Act 2005 s 4)
      `in a townsite` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the place is in a townsite as defined in s 3(1)
      `the control` IS A Control @desc How the dog is being controlled
      `leash length in metres` IS A NUMBER @desc The length of the leash used or carried, in metres from the base of the dog's neck
      `at a show, trial, stock work, hunt or sporting purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether one of the s 31(2)(d)-(h) activities applies: a show, an obedience trial or class, working stock, a foxhound pack, retrieving or duck hunting
GIVETH A `Public place answer, if it arises`
`Was the dog lawfully in the public place where it happened` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `A dog has attacked, chased or threatened me or my animal` THEN `the answer is` (`Is my dog lawfully in this public place` `the dog` `the place` `in the metropolitan region` `in a townsite` `the control` `leash length in metres` `at a show, trial, stock work, hunt or sporting purpose`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`
